Third-party components
----------------------

None. Rally has no third-party dependency and no CDN.

Vendored from this project's own kits (same licence, same author), copied verbatim on 26/11/2026:

- web-kit 0.1.0 — docs/play/web-kit.js — the offline shell, storage helpers and PWA registration
- export-kit 1.0.0 — docs/play/export-kit.js — Blob download, used for the lobby export

Neither kit is modified. Neither makes a network request.

The transport gap
-----------------

A LAN transport does exist in this estate — `lan-kit`, zero dependencies, SSE and POST — but it is not wired into this app. What ships here is a same-device bus, so the room logic runs and can be tested. The engine takes a bus with send/on and ships
with a same-device bus; the demo runs the host and every player in one page through the same lobby rules a
hotspot link would carry. A peer link over the room's network would be a runtime network call, which this
fleet does not make, and faking one would misrepresent the app.

No accounts
-----------

A player is a name and nothing else. There is no password, login, token or account id in this app.
